// ======== Tagged loft: key sections whose features line up ========
//
// 'loftAlong' matches its profiles by the fraction of the whole ring's length, so a feature that moves round
// the section (a corner, a lip line) is smeared between stations. A tagged profile names its feature points
// (tags); 'loftTagged' matches stretch to stretch between the tags, so a tag's column runs from one section's
// tag to the next section's, on the way it is placed, and a crease can sit on a tag's column and fade along the
// run. It also can lay u and v in the surface's own length, so a texture keeps its size.
//
// - Placement is 'loftAlong''s with 'smooth' on: section k at fraction stations[k] of the path's length, in the
//   path's rotation-minimizing frame there (profile x on the frame's normal, y on its binormal), 'between' rings
//   in each band, each column on the Catmull-Rom spline through the sections, knots the stations. With fewer
//   stations than sections they are spread evenly, as 'loftAlong' spreads them.
// - Stretches: the tags cut each profile into stretches, tag i to tag i + 1, and on a closed profile the last
//   tag round to tag 0 (a closed profile with one tag has one stretch, the whole ring). Stretch s of every
//   section corresponds to stretch s of every other. There is no search for a start: tag 0 is the seam of a
//   closed ring, and its column is column 0 (the points before tag 0 close the last stretch).
// - Columns: within each stretch, the union of all sections' point fractions of that stretch's length, as
//   'loft' with count 0 takes them over the whole ring, snapped by LoftSnap, so each section keeps each of its
//   points and a tag's point is its column's, bit for bit.
// - Creases: the edge channel "crease" is always added (0 fill). The edge of tag i's column between ring r
//   and ring r + 1 takes the crease blended linearly between the two sections of its band, at the band's
//   middle fraction; every other edge is 0. Subdivision's semi-sharp rules carry it.
// - Uvs: "uv" is per corner. With 'uvByLength' false they are 'loftAlong''s exactly: u the column's fraction of
//   the ring's length, v the fraction along the path. With it true, u and v are lengths in the mesh's own
//   units: u the distance along the ring (as straight chords between its vertices) from tag 0's column, the
//   closing corners of a closed ring at the ring's whole length; v the distance along the vertex's own column
//   from the first ring (a closed path's closing corners at the column's whole length), so a texture keeps its
//   scale on the outside of a bend as well as the inside; v by the path would stretch the outer side by
//   (radius + offset) / radius. The cap faces keep their 'loftAlong' uvs. Vertex "along" and "around" stay
//   fractions, as every generator writes them.
// - Frames and curve ends ('loftTaggedFramed'): the same stretch matching, creases and uvs, with section k placed in
//   frames[k] (profile x on the frame's normal, y on its binormal) in place of the path's frame, so a section's plane is
//   the caller's. The columns between sections run on the Catmull-Rom spline through the placed points (as 'loft' with
//   frames; knots the frames' origins' distances), where 'loftTagged' blends the profiles and places each blend in the
//   path's frame; with 'between' 0 the two are equal bit for bit when the frames are the path's own at the stations.
//   'startCurve' and 'endCurve' (a 'TaggedCurve') replace the first and last rings: the curve's polyline is cut into
//   stretches by its tags exactly as a section's is, and sampled at the columns' fractions of each stretch (not at the
//   whole ring's), so a tag's point is its column's, bit for bit, and two parts given the one curve and columns of the
//   same fractions per stretch have the same boundary vertices bit for bit (welded at distance 0). The curve takes
//   part in no column; its crease values replace the end section's; an end that is a curve gets no cap. A closed ring
//   of sections that fold through one another, neighbouring sections whose planes' common line cuts both rings with
//   the cut stretches overlapping, gets one problem line naming the first 8 pairs; the mesh is still built.
//   Refusals: a curve whose tag count differs from the sections', with creases not one per tag, with fewer points than
//   tags, or tags not rising or out of range (open: not at both ends); frames and sections of different counts.
// - Ghost sections ('beforeStart', 'afterEnd', a 'GhostSection': a section and its frame): a Catmull-Rom column's slope
//   at an end ring comes from the ring beyond it, which at an end is only a mirror of the ring inside (the end has no
//   neighbour). A ghost is that neighbour: the next section of the part that meets this one at the end, placed in its
//   frame, its stretches cut by its tags and sampled at the columns' fractions like a curve end's. It is used for the
//   slope of the first (last) band's columns and nothing else: no ring, no vertex, no face, no crease, no uv; it adds
//   no column. Its knot is its frame's origin's distance beyond the end section's, as the sections' knots are. Two
//   parts that meet on a shared curve, each holding the other's next section as its ghost, leave the curve with one
//   slope: the Catmull-Rom tangent at the shared ring runs through the same three points (the ring and the two next
//   sections; the knots' spacing is the one thing that can differ). Given neither, everything is as without the
//   feature, bit for bit. Refusals: a ghost whose closedness, tag count, creases, tags or stretch lengths a section
//   would be refused for; a ghost's origin at the end frame's origin.
// - A mirrored half: an open half running from the top midline to the bottom, put through
//   'mirrorWith(..., mirrorU true, uvOffset (-1, 0))', gives the copy u = -u (the copy's u is 1 - u, and the
//   offset takes it to -u): u is continuous across the top midline, and the seam is under the part. No new code.
// - Refusals (one problem line, an empty mesh): fewer than 2 sections or a path of fewer than 2 points; open
//   and closed mixed; tag counts that differ, or creases not one per tag; tags not rising or out of range, or
//   (open) missing either end, or too few (closed 1, open 2); a closed profile not counterclockwise (the loft
//   turns those; with tags a turn would renumber them, so the caller turns it); a stretch of no length (the
//   birth of a tag, which is not built); stations, when given, not rising.

// A profile and its feature points
pub struct TaggedProfile {
  pub profile: Profile;
  // The feature points' numbers, rising. An open profile's first and last points are tags
  pub tags: List[u32];
  // One per tag: the "crease" sharpness of the tag's column at this section; 0 is smooth
  pub creases: List[f32];

  // The profile with these tags and every crease 0
  pub fn of(profile: &Profile, tags: &Array[u32]) TaggedProfile {
    var t = List[u32].withCapacity(tags.len);
    var c = List[f32].withCapacity(tags.len);
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < tags.len {
      t.push(tags[i]);
      c.push(0.);
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    TaggedProfile(Profile(copyList(&profile.points), profile.closed), t, c)
  }
}

// A ring in space with its feature points: the end of a loft that is a 3-D curve ('startCurve', 'endCurve'). Its
// tags correspond to the sections' tags one for one, and it runs the same way round (a closed one) as they do seen
// from ahead; its points need not be coplanar.
pub struct TaggedCurve {
  pub points: List[Vec3];
  // The feature points' numbers, rising; as many as the sections' tags. An open curve's first and last points are tags
  pub tags: List[u32];
  // One per tag: the "crease" sharpness of the tag's column at this end
  pub creases: List[f32];

  // The curve through these points, closed or not, with these tags and every crease 0
  pub fn of(points: &Array[Vec3], tags: &Array[u32]) TaggedCurve {
    var p = List[Vec3].withCapacity(points.len);
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < points.len {
      p.push(points[i]);
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    var t = List[u32].withCapacity(tags.len);
    var c = List[f32].withCapacity(tags.len);
    i = 0usize;
    while i < tags.len {
      t.push(tags[i]);
      c.push(0.);
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    TaggedCurve(p, t, c)
  }
}

// A section and its frame: the neighbouring part's next section, given to a loft for the slope at one end only (see
// "Ghost sections" above). The section has the loft's tag count and closedness.
pub struct GhostSection {
  pub section: TaggedProfile;
  pub frame: Frame;
}

// The ghosts as the core takes them: each placed in space as a curve (its profile's points in its frame, tags kept),
// with its frame's origin, which gives its knot; 'why' is a refusal, or empty
struct GhostRings {
  hasBefore: bool;
  before: TaggedCurve;
  beforeAt: Vec3;
  hasAfter: bool;
  after: TaggedCurve;
  afterAt: Vec3;
  why: String;
}

fn noGhosts() GhostRings {
  GhostRings(false, noCurve(), Vec3(0., 0., 0.), false, noCurve(), Vec3(0., 0., 0.), String.from(""))
}

// A ghost's profile placed in its frame, tags and creases kept
fn placedGhost(g: &GhostSection) TaggedCurve {
  var pts = List[Vec3].withCapacity(g.section.profile.points.len());
  var i = 0usize;
  while i < g.section.profile.points.len() {
    pts.push(g.frame.place(*g.section.profile.points[i]));
    i = i + 1usize;
  }
  TaggedCurve(pts, copyList(&g.section.tags), copyList(&g.section.creases))
}

fn ghostRingsOf(before: &Option[GhostSection], after: &Option[GhostSection], closedLoft: bool) GhostRings {
  var gr = noGhosts();
  match before.asRef() {
    case let Some(g) {
      gr.hasBefore = true;
      gr.before = placedGhost(g);
      gr.beforeAt = g.frame.origin;
      if g.section.profile.closed != closedLoft {
        gr.why = String.from("loftTaggedFramed: the ghost before the start is open where the sections are closed, or the reverse");
      }
    }
    else { }
  }
  match after.asRef() {
    case let Some(g) {
      gr.hasAfter = true;
      gr.after = placedGhost(g);
      gr.afterAt = g.frame.origin;
      if g.section.profile.closed != closedLoft && gr.why.len() == 0usize {
        gr.why = String.from("loftTaggedFramed: the ghost after the end is open where the sections are closed, or the reverse");
      }
    }
    else { }
  }
  gr
}

fn noCurve() TaggedCurve { TaggedCurve(List[Vec3](), List[u32](), List[f32]()) }

fn copyOfCurve(c: &TaggedCurve) TaggedCurve {
  TaggedCurve(copyList(&c.points), copyList(&c.tags), copyList(&c.creases))
}

// The reason a curve cannot end a loft of 'nt' tags, closed or not, or an empty string
fn curveRefusal(c: &TaggedCurve, nt: usize, closed: bool, which: &str) String {
  var why = String.from("loftTaggedFramed: the ");
  why.append(which);
  let m = c.points.len();
  if c.tags.len() != nt {
    why.append(" curve's tag count differs from the sections'");
    return why;
  }
  if c.creases.len() != nt {
    why.append(" curve's creases are not one per tag");
    return why;
  }
  if m < c.tags.len() || (closed && m < 3usize) || (!closed && m < 2usize) {
    why.append(" curve has fewer points than tags");
    return why;
  }
  var i = 0usize;
  while i < nt {
    let t = usize.from(*c.tags[i]);
    if t >= m || (i > 0usize && t <= usize.from(*c.tags[i - 1usize])) {
      why.append(" curve's tags are not rising or out of range");
      return why;
    }
    i = i + 1usize;
  }
  if !closed && (*c.tags[0usize] != 0u32 || usize.from(*c.tags[nt - 1usize]) != m - 1usize) {
    why.append(" curve's first and last points must be tags");
    return why;
  }
  String.from("")
}

// One problem line and an empty mesh
fn taggedRefused(problems: &mut List[String], why: &str) PolyMesh {
  problems.push(String.from(why));
  PolyMesh()
}

// The length of a polyline
fn polyLength(pts: &List[Vec3]) f32 {
  var total: f32 = 0.;
  var j = 1usize;
  while j < pts.len() {
    total = total + pts[j].distance(*pts[j - 1usize]);
    j = j + 1usize;
  }
  total
}

// The tagged loft (see the top of this file). 'caps' closes the end rings of a closed profile by an n-gon each,
// as 'loftAlong''s do. Numbering, ring by ring from the first section: ring r's column j vertex r n + j, n the
// columns, columns in order from tag 0; quads as 'loftAlong''s, then the caps.
pub fn loftTagged(sections: &List[TaggedProfile], path: &Path, stations: &Array[f32], between: u32, uvByLength: bool,
    caps: bool, problems: &mut List[String]) PolyMesh {
  let none = noCurve();
  let noFrames = List[Frame]();
  let noGhost = noGhosts();
  loftTaggedCore(sections, path, stations, &noFrames, false, &none, false, &none, &noGhost, between, uvByLength, caps,
    false, problems)
}

// The tagged loft with each section placed in a frame of its own (see the top of this file, "Frames and curve ends").
// 'frames' one per section (profile x on the frame's normal, y on its binormal); 'startCurve' and 'endCurve', when
// given, are the first and last rings in place of the first and last sections' placed points; 'beforeStart' and
// 'afterEnd', when given, are ghost sections that give the slope at the first and last rings (see "Ghost sections"
// at the top). Numbering as 'loftTagged''s.
pub fn loftTaggedFramed(sections: &List[TaggedProfile], frames: &List[Frame], startCurve: &Option[TaggedCurve],
    endCurve: &Option[TaggedCurve], beforeStart: &Option[GhostSection], afterEnd: &Option[GhostSection], between: u32,
    uvByLength: bool, caps: bool, problems: &mut List[String]) PolyMesh {
  var hasStart = false;
  var hasEnd = false;
  var sc = noCurve();
  var ec = noCurve();
  match startCurve.asRef() {
    case let Some(c) { hasStart = true; sc = copyOfCurve(c); }
    else { }
  }
  match endCurve.asRef() {
    case let Some(c) { hasEnd = true; ec = copyOfCurve(c); }
    else { }
  }
  if frames.len() == 0usize { return taggedRefused(problems, "loftTaggedFramed: no frames"); }
  let noPts = List[Vec3]();
  let noPath = Path.fromPoints(noPts.view(), false);
  let noSt = List[f32]();
  let closedLoft = sections.len() > 0usize && sections[0usize].profile.closed;
  let ghosts = ghostRingsOf(beforeStart, afterEnd, closedLoft);
  loftTaggedCore(sections, &noPath, noSt.view(), frames, hasStart, &sc, hasEnd, &ec, &ghosts, between, uvByLength,
    caps, false, problems)
}

// 'loftTagged', with 'closingStart' allowing one thing it refuses: on a closed profile, the first section's closing
// stretch (the last tag round to tag 0) may have no length, a ring that is closing, its ends meeting (SweepSpec's
// closing part way). That stretch's columns then all start at the one point and open out. With 'frames' not empty
// (one per section) each section is placed in its own frame and the columns between run on the Catmull-Rom spline
// through the placed points; the start and end curves, when 'hasStart' and 'hasEnd', are the first and last rings.
fn loftTaggedCore(sections: &List[TaggedProfile], path: &Path, stations: &Array[f32], frames: &List[Frame],
    hasStart: bool, startC: &TaggedCurve, hasEnd: bool, endC: &TaggedCurve, ghosts: &GhostRings, between: u32,
    uvByLength: bool, caps: bool, closingStart: bool, problems: &mut List[String]) PolyMesh {
  let ns = sections.len();
  let framed = frames.len() > 0usize;
  if ns < 2usize { return taggedRefused(problems, "loftTagged: fewer than 2 sections"); }
  if framed && frames.len() != ns { return taggedRefused(problems, "loftTaggedFramed: frames and sections differ in count"); }
  if !framed && path.points.len() < 2usize { return taggedRefused(problems, "loftTagged: the path has fewer than 2 points"); }
  let closed = sections[0usize].profile.closed;
  let nt = sections[0usize].tags.len();
  var k = 0usize;
  while k < ns {
    if sections[k].profile.closed != closed {
      return taggedRefused(problems, "loftTagged: open and closed profiles mixed");
    }
    if sections[k].tags.len() != nt { return taggedRefused(problems, "loftTagged: the sections' tag counts differ"); }
    if sections[k].creases.len() != nt {
      return taggedRefused(problems, "loftTagged: creases are not one per tag");
    }
    let m = sections[k].profile.points.len();
    if (closed && (m < 3usize || nt < 1usize)) || (!closed && (m < 2usize || nt < 2usize)) {
      return taggedRefused(problems, "loftTagged: too few points or tags");
    }
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < nt {
      let t = usize.from(*sections[k].tags[i]);
      if t >= m || (i > 0usize && t <= usize.from(*sections[k].tags[i - 1usize])) {
        return taggedRefused(problems, "loftTagged: tags not rising or out of range");
      }
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    if !closed && (*sections[k].tags[0usize] != 0u32 || usize.from(*sections[k].tags[nt - 1usize]) != m - 1usize) {
      return taggedRefused(problems, "loftTagged: an open profile's first and last points must be tags");
    }
    if closed && !sections[k].profile.isCounterClockwise() {
      return taggedRefused(problems, "loftTagged: a closed profile must run counterclockwise");
    }
    k = k + 1usize;
  }
  if stations.len >= ns {
    k = 1usize;
    while k < ns {
      if stations[k] <= stations[k - 1usize] { return taggedRefused(problems, "loftTagged: stations not rising"); }
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
  }

  if hasStart {
    let why = curveRefusal(startC, nt, closed, "start");
    if why.len() > 0usize { return taggedRefused(problems, why.view()); }
  }
  if hasEnd {
    let why = curveRefusal(endC, nt, closed, "end");
    if why.len() > 0usize { return taggedRefused(problems, why.view()); }
  }
  if ghosts.why.len() > 0usize { return taggedRefused(problems, ghosts.why.view()); }
  if ghosts.hasBefore {
    let why = curveRefusal(&ghosts.before, nt, closed, "ghost before the start");
    if why.len() > 0usize { return taggedRefused(problems, why.view()); }
  }
  if ghosts.hasAfter {
    let why = curveRefusal(&ghosts.after, nt, closed, "ghost after the end");
    if why.len() > 0usize { return taggedRefused(problems, why.view()); }
  }
  if (hasStart || hasEnd || ghosts.hasBefore || ghosts.hasAfter) && !framed {
    return taggedRefused(problems, "loftTagged: a curve end or a ghost needs frames");
  }

  // Each section's points as Vec3 (z 0), a closed one started at tag 0, and its tags from there. Then the start
  // curve's and the end curve's, as two more rows (they take part in no column, and get the columns' points)
  let startRow = ns;
  let endRow = if hasStart {ns + 1usize} else {ns};
  let beforeRow = endRow + (if hasEnd {1usize} else {0usize});
  let afterRow = beforeRow + (if ghosts.hasBefore {1usize} else {0usize});
  let nsAll = afterRow + (if ghosts.hasAfter {1usize} else {0usize});
  var pts = List[List[Vec3]].withCapacity(nsAll);
  var tg = List[List[usize]].withCapacity(nsAll);
  k = 0usize;
  while k < ns {
    let m = sections[k].profile.points.len();
    var p = List[Vec3].withCapacity(m);
    var j = 0usize;
    while j < m {
      let q = *sections[k].profile.points[j];
      p.push(Vec3(q.x, q.y, 0.));
      j = j + 1usize;
    }
    let shift = if closed {usize.from(*sections[k].tags[0usize])} else {0usize};
    if shift != 0usize { p = rotated(&p, shift); }
    var t = List[usize].withCapacity(nt);
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < nt {
      t.push(usize.from(*sections[k].tags[i]) - shift);
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    pts.push(p);
    tg.push(t);
    k = k + 1usize;
  }
  var ce = 0usize;
  while ce < 4usize {
    if (ce == 0usize && hasStart) || (ce == 1usize && hasEnd) || (ce == 2usize && ghosts.hasBefore)
        || (ce == 3usize && ghosts.hasAfter) {
      let c = if ce == 0usize {startC} else if ce == 1usize {endC} else if ce == 2usize {&ghosts.before} else {&ghosts.after};
      let shift = if closed {usize.from(*c.tags[0usize])} else {0usize};
      var p = copyList(&c.points);
      if shift != 0usize { p = rotated(&p, shift); }
      var t = List[usize].withCapacity(nt);
      var i = 0usize;
      while i < nt {
        t.push(usize.from(*c.tags[i]) - shift);
        i = i + 1usize;
      }
      pts.push(p);
      tg.push(t);
    }
    ce = ce + 1usize;
  }

  // The stretches' polylines and their fractions, section by section
  let nst = if closed {nt} else {nt - 1usize};
  var polys = List[List[Vec3]].withCapacity(nsAll * nst);
  var frs = List[List[f32]].withCapacity(nsAll * nst);
  k = 0usize;
  while k < nsAll {
    let m = pts[k].len();
    var s = 0usize;
    while s < nst {
      let a = *tg[k][s];
      let b = if s + 1usize < nt {*tg[k][s + 1usize]} else {m};
      var poly = List[Vec3].withCapacity(b - a + 1usize);
      var j = a;
      while j <= b {
        poly.push(*pts[k][j % m]);
        j = j + 1usize;
      }
      if !(polyLength(&poly) > 0.) && !(closingStart && closed && k == 0usize && s + 1usize == nst) {
        return taggedRefused(problems, "loftTagged: a stretch between tags has no length");
      }
      frs.push(loopFractions(&poly, false));
      polys.push(poly);
      s = s + 1usize;
    }
    k = k + 1usize;
  }

  // The columns: each stretch's start (its tag), then the union of the sections' interior points' fractions
  var colS = List[usize]();
  var colT = List[f32]();
  var tagCol = List[usize].withCapacity(nt);
  var s = 0usize;
  while s < nst {
    var inner = List[f32]();
    k = 0usize;
    while k < ns {
      let fr = &frs[k * nst + s];
      let cnt = polys[k * nst + s].len();
      var own = List[f32]();
      var j = 1usize;
      while j + 1usize < cnt {
        let t = *fr[j];
        if t > LoftSnap && t < 1. - LoftSnap { own.push(t); }
        j = j + 1usize;
      }
      inner = mergeFractions(&inner, &own);
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
    tagCol.push(colS.len());
    colS.push(s);
    colT.push(0.);
    var q = 0usize;
    while q < inner.len() {
      colS.push(s);
      colT.push(*inner[q]);
      q = q + 1usize;
    }
    s = s + 1usize;
  }
  if !closed {
    tagCol.push(colS.len());
    colS.push(nst - 1usize);
    colT.push(1.);
  }
  let n = colS.len();

  // Each section's ring on the columns, and the columns' fractions of its whole length
  var rings = List[Vec3].withCapacity(nsAll * n);
  var us = List[f32].withCapacity(nsAll * (n + 1usize));
  k = 0usize;
  while k < nsAll {
    var ring = List[Vec3].withCapacity(n);
    var c = 0usize;
    while c < n {
      let sc = *colS[c];
      ring.push(pointAt(&polys[k * nst + sc], &frs[k * nst + sc], false, *colT[c]));
      c = c + 1usize;
    }
    let fr = loopFractions(&ring, closed);
    c = 0usize;
    while c < n {
      rings.push(*ring[c]);
      us.push(*fr[c]);
      c = c + 1usize;
    }
    us.push(1.);
    k = k + 1usize;
  }

  // Placement, as loftAlong's with 'smooth' on
  var knots = List[f32].withCapacity(ns);
  k = 0usize;
  while k < ns {
    if stations.len >= ns { knots.push(stations[k].clamp(0., 1.)); }
    else if path.closed { knots.push(f32.from(k) / f32.from(ns)); }
    else { knots.push(f32.from(k) / f32.from(ns - 1usize)); }
    k = k + 1usize;
  }
  let ringsClosed = !framed && path.closed;
  let pframes = if framed {List[Frame]()} else {path.frames()};
  let dist = if framed {List[f32]()} else {path.distances()};
  let total = if framed {0.} else {path.length()};
  let steps = usize.from(between) + 1usize;
  let bands = if ringsClosed {ns} else {ns - 1usize};
  let nr = if ringsClosed {ns * steps} else {bands * steps + 1usize};
  let first = *knots[0usize];
  let span = *knots[ns - 1usize] - first;
  var pos = List[Vec3].withCapacity(nr * n);
  var ringUs = List[f32].withCapacity(nr * (n + 1usize));
  var vs = List[f32].withCapacity(nr + 1usize);
  var r = 0usize;
  if framed {
    // Each section placed in its own frame; the first and last rings the curves where given; between them the
    // Catmull-Rom spline through the placed points (knots by the frames' origins, as 'loft')
    var sp = List[Vec3].withCapacity(ns * n);
    k = 0usize;
    while k < ns {
      let fr = *frames[k];
      var j = 0usize;
      while j < n {
        let p = *rings[k * n + j];
        sp.push(fr.place(Vec2(p.x, p.y)));
        j = j + 1usize;
      }
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
    if closed { reportCrossings(&sp, frames, n, problems); }
    var j = 0usize;
    while j < n {
      if hasStart { sp.set(j, *rings[startRow * n + j]); }
      if hasEnd { sp.set((ns - 1usize) * n + j, *rings[endRow * n + j]); }
      j = j + 1usize;
    }
    var dsum: f32 = 0.;
    k = 0usize;
    while k < ns {
      if k > 0usize { dsum = dsum + frames[k].origin.distance(frames[k - 1usize].origin); }
      knots.set(k, dsum);
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
    k = 0usize;
    while k < ns {
      if dsum > 0. { knots.set(k, *knots[k] / dsum); }
      else { knots.set(k, f32.from(k) / f32.from(ns - 1usize)); }
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
    // The ghosts, if any, as rows before and after the sections for the splines' slopes (a knot a frame origin's
    // distance beyond the end section's, in the knots' units); kOff is the sections' first row in them
    let kOff = if ghosts.hasBefore {1usize} else {0usize};
    let nsx = ns + kOff + (if ghosts.hasAfter {1usize} else {0usize});
    var spx = List[Vec3].withCapacity(nsx * n);
    var knx = List[f32].withCapacity(nsx);
    if ghosts.hasBefore {
      let d = ghosts.beforeAt.distance(frames[0usize].origin);
      if !(d > 0.) { return taggedRefused(problems, "loftTaggedFramed: the ghost before the start has the first frame's origin"); }
      j = 0usize;
      while j < n {
        spx.push(*rings[beforeRow * n + j]);
        j = j + 1usize;
      }
      knx.push(*knots[0usize] - (if dsum > 0. {d / dsum} else {1. / f32.from(ns - 1usize)}));
    }
    j = 0usize;
    while j < ns * n {
      spx.push(*sp[j]);
      j = j + 1usize;
    }
    k = 0usize;
    while k < ns {
      knx.push(*knots[k]);
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
    if ghosts.hasAfter {
      let d = ghosts.afterAt.distance(frames[ns - 1usize].origin);
      if !(d > 0.) { return taggedRefused(problems, "loftTaggedFramed: the ghost after the end has the last frame's origin"); }
      j = 0usize;
      while j < n {
        spx.push(*rings[afterRow * n + j]);
        j = j + 1usize;
      }
      knx.push(*knots[ns - 1usize] + (if dsum > 0. {d / dsum} else {1. / f32.from(ns - 1usize)}));
    }
    while r < nr {
      let kk = r / steps;
      let i = r % steps;
      let f = f32.from(i) / f32.from(steps);
      let k1 = if kk + 1usize < ns {kk + 1usize} else {kk};
      let ua = rowOf(kk, ns, hasStart, startRow, hasEnd, endRow) * (n + 1usize);
      let ub = rowOf(k1, ns, hasStart, startRow, hasEnd, endRow) * (n + 1usize);
      j = 0usize;
      while j < n {
        pos.push(if i == 0usize {*sp[kk * n + j]} else {columnPoint(&spx, &knx, nsx, n, false, true, kk + kOff, j, f)});
        ringUs.push(if i == 0usize {*us[ua + j]} else {mixf(*us[ua + j], *us[ub + j], f)});
        j = j + 1usize;
      }
      ringUs.push(1.);
      vs.push(if i == 0usize {*knots[kk]} else {mixf(*knots[kk], *knots[k1], f)});
      r = r + 1usize;
    }
    r = nr;
  }
  while r < nr && pframes.len() > 0usize {
    let kk = r / steps;
    let i = r % steps;
    let f = f32.from(i) / f32.from(steps);
    let k1 = (kk + 1usize) % ns;
    let ta = *knots[kk];
    let tb = if i == 0usize {ta} else if k1 == 0usize {*knots[0usize] + 1.} else {*knots[k1]};
    let t = if i == 0usize {ta} else {mixf(ta, tb, f)};
    let fr = frameAtDistance(path, &pframes, &dist, total, t * total);
    var j = 0usize;
    while j < n {
      let p = if i == 0usize {*rings[kk * n + j]}
        else {columnPoint(&rings, &knots, ns, n, path.closed, true, kk, j, f)};
      pos.push(fr.place(Vec2(p.x, p.y)));
      ringUs.push(if i == 0usize {*us[kk * (n + 1usize) + j]}
        else {mixf(*us[kk * (n + 1usize) + j], *us[k1 * (n + 1usize) + j], f)});
      j = j + 1usize;
    }
    ringUs.push(1.);
    if ringsClosed { vs.push(t - first); }
    else if span > 0. { vs.push((t - first) / span); }
    else { vs.push(f32.from(r) / f32.from(nr - 1usize)); }
    r = r + 1usize;
  }
  vs.push(1.);
  if pos.len() == 0usize { return PolyMesh(); }
  let capA = if hasStart {List[Vec2]()} else {ringCapUvs(&rings, 0usize, n, true)};
  let capB = if hasEnd {List[Vec2]()} else {ringCapUvs(&rings, ns - 1usize, n, false)};
  var m = tube(&pos, n, nr, closed, ringsClosed, caps, false, &ringUs, &vs, &capA, &capB);

  // Creases on the tags' columns, by band
  let crease = m.addFloatChannel(EdgeDomain, "crease", 0.);
  let nb = if ringsClosed && nr >= 3usize {nr} else {nr - 1usize};
  r = 0usize;
  while r < nb {
    let kk = r / steps;
    let k1 = (kk + 1usize) % ns;
    let f = (f32.from(r % steps) + 0.5) / f32.from(steps);
    let r1 = (r + 1usize) % nr;
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < nt {
      let a = if kk == 0usize && hasStart {*startC.creases[i]} else {*sections[kk].creases[i]};
      let b = if k1 == ns - 1usize && hasEnd {*endC.creases[i]} else {*sections[k1].creases[i]};
      let c = mixf(a, b, f);
      if c != 0. {
        let col = *tagCol[i];
        let e =edgeBetween(&m, u32.from(r * n + col), u32.from(r1 * n + col));
        if e != NoIndex { m.setFloat(crease, e, c); }
      }
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    r = r + 1usize;
  }

  if uvByLength { setLengthUvs(&mut m, &pos, n, nr, closed, ringsClosed); }
  m
}

// The row of 'rings' and 'us' that holds section k's ring: the section's own, or a curve's at an end
fn rowOf(k: usize, ns: usize, hasStart: bool, startRow: usize, hasEnd: bool, endRow: usize) usize {
  if k == 0usize && hasStart { return startRow; }
  if k + 1usize == ns && hasEnd { return endRow; }
  k
}

// The parameters s = p . d, rising, where the plane through o with normal nrm cuts the closed ring (row 'row' of
// 'sp', n points)
fn planeCuts(sp: &List[Vec3], row: usize, n: usize, o: Vec3, nrm: Vec3, d: Vec3) List[f32] {
  var out = List[f32]();
  var j = 0usize;
  while j < n {
    let a = *sp[row * n + j];
    let b = *sp[row * n + (j + 1usize) % n];
    let da = (a - o).dot(nrm);
    let db = (b - o).dot(nrm);
    if (da < 0. && db >= 0.) || (da >= 0. && db < 0.) {
      let p = a + (b - a) * (da / (da - db));
      let s = p.dot(d);
      out.push(s);
      var q = out.len() - 1usize;
      while q > 0usize && *out[q - 1usize] > *out[q] {
        let t = *out[q - 1usize];
        out[q - 1usize] = *out[q];
        out[q] = t;
        q = q - 1usize;
      }
    }
    j = j + 1usize;
  }
  out
}

// Whether sections k and k + 1 meet inside the part: the line where their planes meet cuts both closed rings, and the
// stretches of it inside each ring overlap (the rings then pass through each other, the part is folded there).
// Parallel planes do not meet.
fn sectionsCross(sp: &List[Vec3], frames: &List[Frame], n: usize, k: usize) bool {
  let fa = *frames[k];
  let fb = *frames[k + 1usize];
  let na = unit(fa.normal.cross(fa.binormal));
  let nb = unit(fb.normal.cross(fb.binormal));
  let d = na.cross(nb);
  if d.length() < 0.000001 { return false; }
  let du = unit(d);
  let ca = planeCuts(sp, k, n, fb.origin, nb, du);
  let cb = planeCuts(sp, k + 1usize, n, fa.origin, na, du);
  if ca.len() % 2usize != 0usize || cb.len() % 2usize != 0usize { return false; }
  var i = 0usize;
  while i + 1usize < ca.len() {
    var j = 0usize;
    while j + 1usize < cb.len() {
      let lo = if *ca[i] > *cb[j] {*ca[i]} else {*cb[j]};
      let hi = if *ca[i + 1usize] < *cb[j + 1usize] {*ca[i + 1usize]} else {*cb[j + 1usize]};
      if hi - lo > 0.00001 { return true; }
      j = j + 2usize;
    }
    i = i + 2usize;
  }
  false
}

// One problem line naming the neighbouring sections that cross (the first 8), if any do
fn reportCrossings(sp: &List[Vec3], frames: &List[Frame], n: usize, problems: &mut List[String]) {
  var count = 0usize;
  var named = String.from("");
  var k = 0usize;
  while k + 1usize < frames.len() {
    if sectionsCross(sp, frames, n, k) {
      if count < 8usize {
        if count > 0usize { named.append(", "); }
        named.appendUInt(u64.from(k));
        named.append("-");
        named.appendUInt(u64.from(k + 1usize));
      }
      count = count + 1usize;
    }
    k = k + 1usize;
  }
  if count > 0usize {
    var line = String.from("loftTaggedFramed: ");
    line.appendUInt(u64.from(count));
    line.append(" neighbouring sections cross inside the part (");
    line.append(named.view());
    if count > 8usize { line.append(", ..."); }
    line.append(")");
    problems.push(line);
  }
}

// The quads' corner uvs in the mesh's own lengths (see the top of this file). The quads are the mesh's first
// faces, band by band, each band's columns in order, as 'tube' makes them.
fn setLengthUvs(m: &mut PolyMesh, pos: &List[Vec3], n: usize, nr: usize, closed: bool, ringsClosed: bool) {
  let pClosed = closed && n >= 3usize;
  let rClosed = ringsClosed && nr >= 3usize;
  // u: the distance along each ring from column 0, and n for the closing one; v: along each column
  var uL = List[f32].withCapacity(nr * (n + 1usize));
  var vL = List[f32].withCapacity(nr * n);
  var vTot = List[f32].withCapacity(n);
  var r = 0usize;
  while r < nr {
    var u: f32 = 0.;
    var j = 0usize;
    while j < n {
      if j > 0usize { u = u + pos[r * n + j].distance(*pos[r * n + j - 1usize]); }
      uL.push(u);
      let v = if r == 0usize {0.} else {*vL[(r - 1usize) * n + j] + pos[r * n + j].distance(*pos[(r - 1usize) * n + j])};
      vL.push(v);
      j = j + 1usize;
    }
    if pClosed { u = u + pos[r * n].distance(*pos[r * n + n - 1usize]); }
    uL.push(u);
    r = r + 1usize;
  }
  var j = 0usize;
  while j < n {
    vTot.push(*vL[(nr - 1usize) * n + j] + pos[j].distance(*pos[(nr - 1usize) * n + j]));
    j = j + 1usize;
  }
  let ch = m.findVec2Channel(CornerDomain, "uv");
  let nb = if rClosed {nr} else {nr - 1usize};
  let nj = if pClosed {n} else {n - 1usize};
  var i = 0usize;
  while i < nb {
    let i1 = i + 1usize;
    let ir = i1 % nr;
    var jj = 0usize;
    while jj < nj {
      let j1 = (jj + 1usize) % n;
      let f = u32.from(i * nj + jj);
      let hs = m.faceHalfedges(f);
      let v1a = if i1 == nr {*vTot[j1]} else {*vL[i1 * n + j1]};
      let v1b = if i1 == nr {*vTot[jj]} else {*vL[i1 * n + jj]};
      m.setVec2(ch, *hs[0usize], Vec2(*uL[i * (n + 1usize) + jj], *vL[i * n + jj]));
      m.setVec2(ch, *hs[1usize], Vec2(*uL[i * (n + 1usize) + jj + 1usize], *vL[i * n + j1]));
      m.setVec2(ch, *hs[2usize], Vec2(*uL[ir * (n + 1usize) + jj + 1usize], v1a));
      m.setVec2(ch, *hs[3usize], Vec2(*uL[ir * (n + 1usize) + jj], v1b));
      jj = jj + 1usize;
    }
    i = i + 1usize;
  }
}
